    "### Hypothesis 2 conclusion: Socioeconomic status → supported\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Health insurance** is the strongest socioeconomic factor: insured respondents have more than double the uptake of uninsured ones (H1N1 31.8% vs 14.7%, seasonal 53.8% vs 22.9%).\n",
    "- **Income:** respondents earning > $75,000 are vaccinated more than those below poverty (H1N1 25.3% vs 19.1%, seasonal 49.7% vs 36.3%).\n",
    "- **Housing:** owners are vaccinated more than renters (seasonal 50.1% vs 37.1%).\n",
    "- **Note:** 46% of `health_insurance` answers are missing. This \"Unknown\" group has very low H1N1 uptake (11.3%), so missingness itself carries information.\n",
    "- **Verdict:** higher socioeconomic status, especially having health insurance, goes with higher vaccine uptake."
   ]
